    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332-a1">

                <pb facs="0780" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg766"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smythe, Collector,
                        to Mr. Courtney, district attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House, New
                            York</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-02-05"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">February</hi> 5, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[16]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to report the seizure, on the 2d
                    instant, of the steamship R. R. Cuyler, and request that proceedings may be
                    instituted for the forfeiture thereof, together with her tackle, apparel,
                    &amp;c., under the third section of the neutrality act of April 20, 1818. I
                    inclose the report of the surveyor of the port who made the seizure and
                    examination as therein related, together with the register, manifest, crew-list,
                    shipping articles, clearance, bill of health, and letter of instructions *to the
                    master, the papers taken from the rooms of the captain and his assistant, and
                    the affidavits referred to by the surveyor, and four drawings taken from the
                    vessel but not mentioned in the report.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. A. SMYTHE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. G. Courtney</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Attorney.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
